     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This is all very exciting Inacki - the package has grown substantially since I started with it in the Spring.  <div><br></div><div>Good work!</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Jul 5, 2016 at 9:29 AM, Iñaki Úcar <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">i.uc...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Until now, the prioritization values (<code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">priority</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">preemptible</code>, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">restart</code>) were assigned to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">seize</code> activities, and they were static values, so it was not possible to change them dynamically through a function, as Cameron was trying to do in <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/simmer-devel/Avssvd6loHo/1DEtg5m7AAAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/simmer-devel/Avssvd6loHo/1DEtg5m7AAAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467974154000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06AINUfm15UL81UKKeOTXX\">this thread</a>.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Now, I’ve moved the prioritization definition to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">add_generator</code>, which has several advantages:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Symmetry with <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">add_resource</code>, which defines resource <em>preemptiveness</em>.</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">Simpler syntax for <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">seize</code>.</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">More natural interpretation of prioritization values as attributes of arrivals from the same generator, rather than attributes of a <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">seize</code>.</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\">More flexibility, since there is a new activity called <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">set_prioritization</code>, which accepts a custom function as well as static parameters, to change these values dynamically inside the trajectory.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">See <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/69#issuecomment-230149192\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/69%23issuecomment-230149192&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467974154000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ApgoMUOUK_OVu1S-D0tqp\">#69</a> for more information and working examples.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Many models require an arrival to do something if it gets rejected when trying to seize a resource. Some time ago, I had proposed a new activity called <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">ifseize</code> to cover this requirement. As #69 alleviates <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">seize</code>‘s syntax, I’ve finally decided to add this feature to <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">seize</code> itself (and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">seize_selected</code>).</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">The implementation and general operation have a lot in common with a <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">branch</code>. In this case, you can define two optional subtrajectories:</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">post.seize</code>: if present, it’s executed after a successful seize. As in a <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">branch</code>, a flag <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">continue</code> controls whether the arrival must continue in the main trajectory or not.</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">reject</code>: if present, it’s executed after an unsuccessful seize (a rejection). Instead of getting dropped, the arrival follows this subtrajectory and, again, a flag <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">continue</code> controls whether the subtrajectory must be linked to the main trajectory.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">See <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49#issuecomment-230466052\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/49%23issuecomment-230466052&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467974154000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3UXZ9JQnPuIfDOx1Ub38wI\">#49</a> for more information and working examples.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Finally, I’d like to share some numbers with you. I’m proud that we have reached 50 closed issues on GitHub, 19 of them since this mailing list was created. This list has proved to be a great source of feedback. So thank you all, and spread the word of simmer. ;-)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Regards,</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgYWxsLDxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+VW50aWwgbm93LCB0aGUgcHJpb3JpdGl6YXRpb24g\r\ndmFsdWVzIChgcHJpb3JpdHlgLCBgcHJlZW1wdGlibGVgLCBgcmVzdGFydGApIHdlcmUgYXNzaWdu\r\nZWQgdG8gYHNlaXplYCBhY3Rpdml0aWVzLCBhbmQgdGhleSB3ZXJlIHN0YXRpYyB2YWx1ZXMsIHNv\r\nIGl0IHdhcyBub3QgcG9zc2libGUgdG8gY2hhbmdlIHRoZW0gZHluYW1pY2FsbHkgdGhyb3VnaCBh\r\nIGZ1bmN0aW9uLCBhcyBDYW1lcm9uIHdhcyB0cnlpbmcgdG8gZG8gaW4gW3RoaXMgdGhyZWFkXSho\r\ndHRwczovL2dyb3Vwcy5nb29nbGUuY29tL2QvbXNnL3NpbW1lci1kZXZlbC9BdnNzdmQ2bG9Iby8x\r\nREV0ZzVtN0FBQUopLjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Tm93LCBJJ3ZlIG1vdmVkIHRo\r\nZSBwcmlvcml0aXphdGlvbiBkZWZpbml0aW9uIHRvIGBhZGRfZ2VuZXJhdG9yYCwgd2hpY2ggaGFz\r\nIHNldmVyYWwgYWR2YW50YWdlczo8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiogU3ltbWV0cnkg\r\nd2l0aCBgYWRkX3Jlc291cmNlYCwgd2hpY2ggZGVmaW5lcyByZXNvdXJjZSBfcHJlZW1wdGl2ZW5l\r\nc3NfLjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+KiBTaW1wbGVyIHN5bnRheCBmb3IgYHNlaXplYC48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Piog\r\nTW9yZSBuYXR1cmFsIGludGVycHJldGF0aW9uIG9mIHByaW9yaXRpemF0aW9uIHZhbHVlcyBhcyBh\r\ndHRyaWJ1dGVzIG9mIGFycml2YWxzIGZyb20gdGhlIHNhbWUgZ2VuZXJhdG9yLCByYXRoZXIgdGhh\r\nbiBhdHRyaWJ1dGVzIG9mIGEgYHNlaXplYC48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiogTW9yZSBmbGV4aWJpbGl0eSwg\r\nc2luY2UgdGhlcmUgaXMgYSBuZXcgYWN0aXZpdHkgY2FsbGVkIGBzZXRfcHJpb3JpdGl6YXRpb25g\r\nLCB3aGljaCBhY2NlcHRzIGEgY3Vz